  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"57\" data-end=\"330\"><strong data-start=\"57\" data-end=\"86\">Free Androgen Index (FAI)</strong> is a calculated ratio that estimates the amount of <strong data-start=\"138\" data-end=\"168\">biologically active (free)</strong> testosterone in the blood. It is especially useful in evaluating <strong data-start=\"234\" data-end=\"262\">androgen status in women</strong>, where direct measurement of free testosterone is often unreliable.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1460\"><strong data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1460\">FAI in Clinical Context</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1853\">\n<li data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1705\">\n<p data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1477\"><strong data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1476\">In Women</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1705\">\n<li data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1531\">\n<p data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1531\">FAI is a <strong data-start=\"1491\" data-end=\"1530\">screening tool for hyperandrogenism</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1534\" data-end=\"1641\">\n<p data-start=\"1536\" data-end=\"1641\">Elevated FAI is often seen in <strong data-start=\"1566\" data-end=\"1574\">PCOS</strong>, especially if SHBG is low (due to obesity or insulin resistance).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1644\" data-end=\"1705\">\n<p data-start=\"1646\" data-end=\"1705\">A high FAI is more sensitive than total testosterone alone.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1707\" data-end=\"1853\">\n<p data-start=\"1709\" data-end=\"1720\"><strong data-start=\"1709\" data-end=\"1719\">In Men</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1723\" data-end=\"1853\">\n<li data-start=\"1723\" data-end=\"1853\">\n<p data-start=\"1725\" data-end=\"1853\">Used less frequently, but low FAI may indicate <strong data-start=\"1772\" data-end=\"1795\">androgen deficiency</strong>, especially if SHBG is high (e.g., aging, liver disease).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>FAI</strong> Level</th>\n<th><strong>Possible Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low FAI</strong></td>\n<td>- Hypogonadism (in men) - Androgen deficiency - Elevated SHBG (e.g., from liver disease, estrogen therapy)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal FAI</strong></td>\n<td>- Normal androgen status</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High FAI (especially in women)</strong></td>\n<td>- <strong>Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS)</strong> - <strong>Hirsutism</strong>, <strong>acne</strong>, <strong>infertility</strong> - Androgen-secreting tumor - <strong>Congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH)</strong> - <strong>Insulin resistance / obesity</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"57\" data-end=\"330\">&nbsp;</p>",
